// An `is` test selects WHICH variant; the mutability comes from the SCRUTINEE,
// never from the type written in the test. Both variants here are read-only, so
// the narrowed `i32[]` is read-only too and `push` is T3071 — reported on the
// push, at the right place, rather than swallowed by a T3040 "test can never
// match" on the test itself (which is what happened while the overlap check
// still compared mutability).
//
// The mirror case — a union of MUTABLE variants, where the same push is legal —
// is `tests/snippets/union_variant_narrow_mutation`.
module "snippet"

fill :: fn(x: i32[] | string[]) -> usize {
    if x is i32[] {
        x.push(0)
        return x.len()
    }
    return x.len()
}

main :: fn() -> i32 = i32(fill([1, 2]))
